              "id": "CVE-2020-15095",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2020-15095: Insertion of Sensitive Information into Log File"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2020-15095?s=github&n=npm&t=npm&vr=%3C6.14.6",
              "help": {
                "text": "Versions of the npm CLI prior to 6.14.6 are vulnerable to an information exposure vulnerability through log files. The CLI supports URLs like `<protocol>://[<user>[:<password>]@]<hostname>[:<port>][:][/]<path>`. The password value is not redacted and is printed to stdout and also to any generated log files.\n",
                "markdown": "> Versions of the npm CLI prior to 6.14.6 are vulnerable to an information exposure vulnerability through log files. The CLI supports URLs like `<protocol>://[<user>[:<password>]@]<hostname>[:<port>][:][/]<path>`. The password value is not redacted and is printed to stdout and also to any generated log files.\n\n|                                                                                                  |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:npm/npm@6.2.0  |\n|Affected range                                                                 <6.14.6            |\n|Fixed version                                                                  6.14.6             |\n|[[CVSS Score 4.4] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N]]                     |\n"
