            {
              "id": "CVE-2020-7608",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2020-7608: Improperly Controlled Modification of Object Prototype Attributes ('Prototype Pollution')"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2020-7608?s=github&n=yargs-parser&t=npm&vr=%3E%3D6.0.0%2C%3C13.1.2",
              "help": {
                "text": "Affected versions of `yargs-parser` are vulnerable to prototype pollution. Arguments are not properly sanitized, allowing an attacker to modify the prototype of `Object`, causing the addition or modification of an existing property that will exist on all objects.  \nParsing the argument `--foo.__proto__.bar baz'` adds a `bar` property with value `baz` to all objects. This is only exploitable if attackers have control over the arguments being passed to `yargs-parser`.\n\n\n\n## Recommendation\n\nUpgrade to versions 13.1.2, 15.0.1, 18.1.1 or later.\n",
                "markdown": "> Affected versions of `yargs-parser` are vulnerable to prototype pollution. Arguments are not properly sanitized, allowing an attacker to modify the prototype of `Object`, causing the addition or modification of an existing property that will exist on all objects.  \nParsing the argument `--foo.__proto__.bar baz'` adds a `bar` property with value `baz` to all objects. This is only exploitable if attackers have control over the arguments being passed to `yargs-parser`.\n\n\n\n## Recommendation\n\nUpgrade to versions 13.1.2, 15.0.1, 18.1.1 or later.\n\n|                                                                                                           |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:npm/yargs-parser@9.0.2  |\n|Affected range                                                                 >=6.0.0,<13.1.2             |\n|Fixed version                                                                  13.1.2                      |\n|[[CVSS Score 5.3] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L]]                              |\n"
              },
