            {
              "id": "CVE-2020-36604",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2020-36604: Improperly Controlled Modification of Object Prototype Attributes ('Prototype Pollution')"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2020-36604?s=github&n=hoek&t=npm&vr=%3C%3D6.1.3",
              "help": {
                "text": "hoek versions prior to 8.5.1, and 9.x prior to 9.0.3 are vulnerable to prototype pollution in the clone function. If an object with the __proto__ key is passed to clone() the key is converted to a prototype. This issue has been patched in version 9.0.3, and backported to 8.5.1.\n",
                "markdown": "> hoek versions prior to 8.5.1, and 9.x prior to 9.0.3 are vulnerable to prototype pollution in the clone function. If an object with the __proto__ key is passed to clone() the key is converted to a prototype. This issue has been patched in version 9.0.3, and backported to 8.5.1.\n\n|                                                                                                    |\n|Package                                                                        pkg:npm/hoek@2.16.3  |\n|Affected range                                                                 <=6.1.3              |\n|Fixed version                                                                  not fixed            |\n|[[CVSS Score 8.1] [CVSS Vector CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H]]                       |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
