              "id": "CVE-2017-17458",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2017-17458: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2017-17458?s=github&n=mercurial&t=pypi&vr=%3C4.4.1",
              "help": {
                "text": "In Mercurial before 4.4.1, it is possible that a specially malformed repository can cause Git subrepositories to run arbitrary code in the form of a `.git/hooks/post-update` script checked into the repository. Typical use of Mercurial prevents construction of such repositories, but they can be created programmatically.\n",
                "markdown": "> In Mercurial before 4.4.1, it is possible that a specially malformed repository can cause Git subrepositories to run arbitrary code in the form of a `.git/hooks/post-update` script checked into the repository. Typical use of Mercurial prevents construction of such repositories, but they can be created programmatically.\n\n|                                                                                                                            |\n|Package                                                                                           pkg:pypi/mercurial@3.1.2  |\n|Affected range                                                                                    <4.4.1                    |\n|Fixed version                                                                                     4.4.1                     |\n|[[CVSS Score 9.3] [CVSS Vector CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N]]                            |\n"
